nse fields make two edited field lists easy to disagree. ## Decision Generate the factual reference from the versioned contract. ## Reasoning Keep names, types and defaults tied to one source. ## Consequences We must run generation and inspect its result when the contract changes. Explanations and examples still need human review. ## Alternatives Keep editing the field list by hand, accepting the duplicate review work. ``` Preserve the historical decision text. Append a dated supersession notice to the old record, link it to the replacement, and link back from the new one. The old acceptance status is historical; the later notice makes its current status clear. Update an existing decision index too. A new decision must not rewrite an earlier choice to make the team look prescient. This extends the small-record approach in [Nygard’s ADR guidance](https://cognitect.com/blog/2011/11/15/documenting-architecture-decisions) with an explicit append-only notice for this playbook’s preservation convention. "

